  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 234 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThe remnant moisture from Tropical Storm Edouard will drift \ntoward north Central Texas Thursday morning. Some of the guidance \nis indicating that the remnant moisture will then drift west on \nthe western periphery of an upper level ridge centered across the \nSoutheast United States. This may result in the development of at \nleast isolated afternoon showers and thunderstorms Thursday \nafternoon and Friday afternoon. Continued low end (15-20%) rain \nchances for now. Highs Thursday and Friday will be hot, in the \nupper 90s to near 104. \n\nDrier conditions return next weekend as the upper level ridge \nrepositions itself across the Southern Plains. Highs will continue\nto be above seasonal normals, in the mid 90s to near 101.",
